.TH PHX-DEMO-CTL 1 "2026-09-05" "Phalanx Duel" "Phalanx Duel Local Tooling"
.SH NAME
phx-demo-ctl \- rehearse the host-native Phalanx Duel demo
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B phx-demo-ctl
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B phx-demo-ctl
starts and inspects the local server, browser client, and admin UI. It expects
Postgres on the host and does not start Docker or Colima implicitly.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B up
Start the demo services, wait for readiness, and open the cockpit.
.TP
.B down
Stop demo services and the cockpit bridge.
.TP
.B restart
Stop and start the demo services, then wait for readiness.
.TP
.B status
Print a one-shot health snapshot.
.TP
.B reset
Reset the development rehearsal state.
.TP
.B logs
Tail the local service logs.
.TP
.B links
Generate or refresh the browser cockpit.
.TP
.B restart-cockpit
Restart only the browser cockpit bridge, leaving game services running.
.TP
.B cockpit
Run the interactive terminal dashboard.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --no-open
Do not open a browser window.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show usage and exit successfully.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PHALANX_DEMO_COCKPIT_PORT
Cockpit bridge port; defaults to 3333.
.TP
.B PHALANX_DEMO_READY_TIMEOUT
Service readiness timeout; defaults to 60 seconds.
.TP
.B PHALANX_DEMO_JAEGER_URL
Jaeger base URL used by the generated cockpit; defaults to
https://jaeger.localhost.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B .phx/logs/
Host-native service logs and cockpit.log.
.TP
.B output/demo/OBSERVABILITY-PAIRING.md
Presenter packet for the OpenObserve and Jaeger telemetry walkthrough.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR phx-services (1),
.BR phx (1),
.BR phx-dock (1)
